assertion_line: 24
expression: login.render_long_help().to_string()
---
Manage login

Usage: airs login [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  status  Show login status
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --restore-session
          Restore the verified OIDC identity without invalidating this environment's open sessions

      --issuer-url <ISSUER_URL>
          HTTPS issuer for a public-client OIDC login

      --oidc-client-id <OIDC_CLIENT_ID>
          

      --audience <AUDIENCE>
          Resource audience required in the signed gateway access token

      --credential-file <CREDENTIAL_FILE>
          Reference an existing owner-only credential file (explicit headless mode)

      --credential-env <CREDENTIAL_ENV>
          Reference a credential environment variable; nothing secret is persisted

      --with-api-key
          Enter a workspace API key at a hidden terminal prompt and save it in the OS credential
          store. Automation may supply the key through stdin. The key is never saved in a plaintext
          configuration file.

      --device-auth
          

      --no-browser
          Print the company login URL without opening the desktop browser

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
